# systemd EnvironmentFile syntax: KEY=value, with quotes around values containing
# spaces. This is not a shell script. Keep this file owned by root with mode 0600.
# Installation leaves the service stopped and disabled. Configure LDAP first,
# then run: systemctl enable --now devbox-kvm.service

DATA_ROOT_DIR=/var/lib/devbox-kvm
LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8443
PUBLIC_ADDRESS=localhost:8443

# For remote access, set LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8443 and PUBLIC_ADDRESS to the public
# hostname and port. HTTPS and RDP share the listener; use direct TCP routing.
# The native service prepares VM_CGROUP_ROOT automatically; do not set it here.

# Required authentication settings; uncomment and adapt for your directory.
# LDAP_URL=ldaps://directory.example.com
# LDAP_BASE_DN=dc=example,dc=com
# LDAP_USER_DOMAIN=example.com
# LDAP_USERNAME_ATTRIBUTE=sAMAccountName
# LDAP_USER_FILTER=(userPrincipalName=%s)
# LDAP_REQUIRED_GROUP="CN=Desktop Users,OU=Groups,DC=example,DC=com"
# ADMIN_GROUP="CN=Desktop Admins,OU=Groups,DC=example,DC=com"
# LDAP_CA_FILE=/etc/devbox-kvm/directory-ca.pem

# Without TLS settings the gateway creates a persistent self-signed certificate.
# Configure trusted TLS before exposing the listener to remote clients.
# CERT_FILE=/etc/devbox-kvm/fullchain.pem
# KEY_FILE=/etc/devbox-kvm/key.pem
# ACME_ENABLE=true
# ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# See /usr/share/doc/devbox-kvm/configuration.md for all environment settings.
# If you increase VM_STOP_TIMEOUT, also increase TimeoutStopSec in a service
# drop-in to allow at least six additional seconds for worker cleanup.
